I suggested a means of creating an altar a while back. It didn't go
down too well.

My suggested method was somewhat more difficult than the one suggested
here:

First you had to gather/ create anything from 4 to >100 (depending in
monster difficulty: weak monsters require more) blessed statues of your
preferred monster type.

Then you had to arrange them in a particular pattern (which in most
cases would require digging out most of the level) in a feature-free
area of the dungeon.

Then you had to piss off your own god by praying and creating a temple
(with priest) to the [monster] God. For example, if you had chosen to
gather Orc statues, you would create a temple to the Orc God. These
monster Gods would be a new addition to the game, but would have no
role outside of this temple-creation procedure. Monster altars would
behave much like any cross-aligned altar.

Assuming you want to convert the altar, you now have to go away and get
back in your God's good books before you can even attempt it.

Finally, when you do convert the altar, you have to fight off not only
the priest, but all the statues you gathered, which are brought to life
by the vengeful deity.

I think nethack does need something that allows the player to create an
altar, but it shouldn't be easy=-)


